# V11.E item (b) — graphiti probe graceful-skip (Resolution A)

2026-05-03. v0.1.2 item per `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-x-roadmap.md`
§2 v0.1.2 item 2 (item-b-only — items (a) and (c) verified
already-fixed at f0c4aa9 per prior V11.E status).

Sub-plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-2-V11-E-graphiti-probe-skip.md`.
Predecessor status: `<pos3>/workspace/.scratch/claude-output/
v11e-followon-hazards-status-2026-05-03.md` (4-option matrix +
Resolution A justification).

Scope (per sub-plan §4 + §6): two-component fence on
`framework/orchestrator/` + `framework/primary-persona/`. Source
edits gate both session-start memory probe sites on the existence
of `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.loam.memory-graphiti.plist`. M-FBM-
only stranger workspaces (no graphiti installed → no plist) see
`memory: not_expected` instead of `memory: down`; status `ready`
instead of `partial`; exit_code 0 instead of 3.

Resolution A choice rationale (per prior V11.E status §item (b)):
minimum-surface (ranked over Resolutions B/C/D); uses existing
source-of-truth (`ask_service_manager_to_start` already inspects
the same plist); self-correcting for future M-GMP (graphiti as
plugin in v0.2) — when the user installs graphiti, the plist
appears and probing re-engages naturally with no further code
change.

AC surface (per sub-plan §4):

  - AC.V11.E.1 — `pos_session_start.run_session_start` consults
    the plist before invoking `probe_memory_fn`; absent → skip;
    `memory_expected: False` in result; `additional_context`
    warning text drops the `memory_up=...` token. Verified by
    new tests `test_AC_V11_E_1_*` + smoke A.
  - AC.V11.E.2 — `session_start_gate._probe_memory` returns the
    sentinel `"not_expected"` when the plist is absent; existing
    `dict[str, str]` schema admits the new string value (no
    schema change). Verified by new test file
    `test_AC_V11_E_2_probe_memory_skips_when_plist_absent.py`
    + smoke C.
  - AC.V11.E.3 — both probe sites use the SAME canonical location
    (`Path.home() / "Library" / "LaunchAgents" /
    "com.loam.memory-graphiti.plist"`). Verified by direct file
    read post-fix + the new test
    `test_AC_V11_E_3_canonical_plist_path_matches_orchestrator_helper`.
  - AC.V11.E.4 — negative AC: plist-present scenario reports
    identical behaviour to pre-fix (memory_up/down per probe
    outcome). Verified by smokes B + D and by the existing tests
    passing without any behaviour-pinning regression.
  - AC.V11.E.S — fence: `framework/orchestrator/` +
    `framework/primary-persona/` only; plus
    `docs/rebuild/plans/` via universal prefix.

Smokes captured pre-seal (verbatim):

    === Smoke A: pos_session_start, plist absent ===
    status: ready
    memory_up: True
    memory_expected: False
    exit_code: 0
    additional_context: pos v2 ready

    === Smoke B: plist PRESENT, memory down ===
    status: partial
    memory_up: False
    memory_expected: True
    exit_code: 3
    additional_context: pos v2 session-start: services did not come
        up within 0s (memory_up=False, orchestrator_up=True).
        Supervisor will escalate loudly on start. Warnings:
        com.loam.orchestrator.plist not installed at /tmp/v11e-
        smoke/present-launchagents/com.loam.orchestrator.plist.

    === Smoke C: gate _probe_memory, plist absent ===
    memory: not_expected
    orchestrator: unknown

    === Smoke D: gate _probe_memory, plist PRESENT ===
    memory: up
    orchestrator: unknown

All four contracts (per AC.V11.E.{1,2,4}) pass: plist-absent
skips probe + reports not_expected/memory_expected=False; plist-
present preserves legacy probe behaviour.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - `memory_up` semantic in result-dict: reports the not-blocking
    state — True when probed-and-up OR when not-expected
    (graceful skip). `memory_expected` disambiguates the two
    cases for callers that need to distinguish (e.g.,
    observability). This preserves existing-consumer compat
    (consumers reading `memory_up` see "not blocking"); the
    `memory_expected` field is additive for new consumers.
  - Sentinel string `not_expected` chosen over `n/a` / omit-
    from-dict because:
      * the prior status file's owner-ruling matrix recommended
        `not_expected` for the gate (retains architectural-state
        visibility in the rendered service_state block);
      * existing `dict[str, str]` schema admits arbitrary
        strings (verified by reading `context_composer.py:165`).
  - `ask_service_manager_to_start` not modified — instead, the
    memory-label "plist not installed" warning is filtered from
    the `additional_context` string in the not-expected case
    (Surface #4). The warning is still informative when memory
    IS expected (real problem) but is filtered as noise in the
    M-FBM case (expected state).
  - Existing tests in `test_pos_session_start.py` opt into
    legacy "memory expected" semantics by passing
    `is_memory_expected_fn=lambda: True` (4 sites). This is
    in-fence test sidecar; preserves the test behaviour and
    clarifies the new-default vs legacy semantics.

Out of scope (per sub-plan §9):

  - Items (a) corpus_gate fallback + (c) plist template module
    name (verified already-fixed at f0c4aa9 per prior V11.E
    status).
  - Workspace-config flag for memory provider (Resolution D;
    deferred to v0.1.5 D-3 / v0.2 M-GMP).
  - Inventory-driven probe set (Resolution B; rejected).
  - Removing memory probe entirely (Resolution C; rejected).
  - Renaming `memory_up` → `memory_expected` (additive only).

Predecessor commits:
  - f0c4aa9 — items (a) and (c) of original V11.E (plist template
    module name + corpus_gate fallback).
  - 9d58062 — V11.A seal (orchestrator runtime fix).
  - 4cfeae4 — bug-investigation template (BASELINE for V11.E).

